From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: retry a native guest fault during PS4 exec migration (archive 1011 + 1015).

Archive 1011 and 1015 as one change, applied with git apply --recount.
ABI-v4 ntdll still migrates exec pages from direct to flexible memory
(src/native/pw_wine_dmem_glue_ps4.c), but nothing called the fault-side
half, __wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration, and upstream's S/1000 retry runs
only under wowprospero's hook, so native WoW64 had no guest-fault retry.
1015 passes the page-fault error code as the glue's third argument.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index a281233..8e814c2 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -2827,6 +2827,22 @@ static void __attribute__((used)) segv_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo,
             unsigned int n = __atomic_add_fetch( &trace_count, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED );
             BOOL handled, invalid_gs;
 
+            /* A PS4 direct-memory RX migration can briefly leave a guest
+             * page unmapped while it is replaced with flexible memory. If a
+             * guest thread faults on that exact page during the replacement,
+             * wait for the mapping operation and retry the instruction only
+             * when its requested access is valid in the settled mapping. */
+            extern int __wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration( const void *, unsigned int,
+                                                            unsigned int ) __attribute__((weak));
+            if (__wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration &&
+                __wine_ps5_wait_for_exec_migration( siginfo->si_addr,
+                                                     (unsigned int)rec.ExceptionInformation[0],
+                                                     (unsigned int)ERROR_sig(sigcontext) ))
+            {
+                leave_handler( data, sigcontext );
+                return;
+            }
+
             if (n <= 12)
             {
                 extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
